WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.768
Welcome to our training on virtual bundles.

00:00:02.768 --> 00:00:09.096
Amazon customers often shop for multiple items at once and use brands to help identify products

00:00:09.096 --> 00:00:10.282
that go together.

00:00:10.282 --> 00:00:15.819
A flower pot and a pack of seeds, for example, or shampoo and conditioner.

00:00:15.819 --> 00:00:22.542
To make it easier for customers to find and purchase related products, we created the Virtual Bundles

00:00:22.542 --> 00:00:22.937
program.

00:00:22.937 --> 00:00:29.660
A virtual bundle is a group of two to five products on a single product detail page.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:36.300
The individual products are all part of the same brand and are available on their own product detail

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:37.000
pages too.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:42.000
But the virtual bundle allows customers to purchase them as a group.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:46.000
Let's find out how brands create virtual bundles.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:52.000
Before we review the process, let's go over a few key requirements and conditions.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:56.000
There are two basic requirements for all virtual bundles.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:02.650
The first is that the products they contain need to be part of a brand enrolled in Amazon brand

00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:03.000
registry.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:08.000
The seller who creates a bundle needs to be internal to the brand too.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:14.588
If you'd like more information about brand registry and access to brand selling benefits like virtual

00:01:14.588 --> 00:01:15.000
bundles,

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:22.000
see the series of modules in our Seller University course, launch your brand in the Amazon store.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:29.391
The second basic requirement for virtual bundles is that the products they contain need to be shipped

00:01:29.391 --> 00:01:32.000
through fulfillment by Amazon or FBA.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:38.000
The seller who creates the bundle also needs to have an FBA account in good standing.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:44.967
Your FBA products must be in new condition too, and they can't be a gift card or an electronically

00:01:44.967 --> 00:01:49.000
delivered item like digital music, a video or an e-book.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:55.400
When a customer orders a virtual bundle through FBA, each item is fulfilled separately, just like

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:57.000
for a standard order.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:01.000
We don't charge additional FBA or selling fees.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:07.000
Sellers don't have to package products together or make any other changes to their inventory either.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:13.261
The quantity of virtual bundles you have in stock is determined by the smallest quantity available

00:02:13.261 --> 00:02:16.000
for an individual product in the bundle.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:23.378
For example, if you sell a bundle that contains a dart board and a set of 5 darts, and you have

00:02:23.378 --> 00:02:26.892
10 dart boards and 15 sets of darts in stock,

00:02:26.892 --> 00:02:29.000
you'll have 10 virtual bundles available.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:37.000
All 25 of your products will still be stored separately in our fulfillment centers and available

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:39.000
for individual purchase too.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:45.045
When a customer buys one of your 10 dart boards, you'll have 9 dart boards and 9 virtual bundles

00:02:45.045 --> 00:02:46.000
left in stock.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:53.200
And when another customer buys your bundle, you'll have 8 bundles, 8 dart boards, and 14 sets of

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:54.000
darts left.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:03:02.000
In addition to the requirements for brand registry and FBA, virtual bundles need to meet a few conditions.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:06.000
First, they need to be organized around a main product.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:12.800
We use this main product to drive searches for your virtual bundle, which means its keywords become

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:14.000
the bundle's keywords.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:21.000
Other attributes from the main product, like category, are also carried over to your bundle.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:26.000
The same main product can be used to create multiple virtual bundles.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:32.000
For example, a t-shirt could be bundled 4 times with 4 different pairs of pants from your brand.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:37.950
But make sure you don't create bundles that contain the same group of products with a different

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:39.000
main product assigned.

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:45.514
Don't create a bundle with a t-shirt as a main product, and pants as another product, then create

00:03:45.514 --> 00:03:48.257
a second bundle with the same two items

00:03:48.257 --> 00:03:51.000
that uses the pants as the main product.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:56.000
It's also important to note that sellers can't create virtual bundles as variations.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:04:02.632
If you want to create bundles that contain different versions of a product, for color or size, for

00:04:02.632 --> 00:04:03.000
example,

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:10.000
create a separate bundle for each version rather than trying to establish variation relationships.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:16.222
In addition, each virtual bundle you create needs to contain two to five different products within

00:04:16.222 --> 00:04:17.000
your brand.

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:24.000
A virtual bundle can't be a group of the same product, like a multi-pack, case pack, or pallet.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:30.000
Virtual bundles can contain multiple units of a single product in combination with other products.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:36.967
For example, a virtual bundle could contain two of the same coffee mugs, as long as it also included

00:04:36.967 --> 00:04:41.000
other products like a bag of coffee and a coffee pot.

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:46.684
It's important to note, however, that you can't have multiple units of a main product in a virtual

00:04:46.684 --> 00:04:47.000
bundle.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:54.273
In our example, either the bag of coffee or the coffee pot could be the main product, but the two

00:04:54.273 --> 00:04:55.000
mugs couldn't.

00:04:55.000 --> 00:05:01.000
Make sure the products you include in a bundle are also complementary and compatible.

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:04.000
Group products that are used together.

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:09.368
And if you're bundling products like a phone and charging cable, make sure they're designed to be

00:05:09.368 --> 00:05:10.000
used together.

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:16.667
The last condition for a virtual bundle is that its price needs to be either the same as the total

00:05:16.667 --> 00:05:19.000
price for the products in the bundle,

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:25.000
or lower if you'd like to offer customers a discount for purchasing multiple items at once.

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:29.000
Remember that reduced prices can help attract customers.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:34.667
If the price of an individual product in your virtual bundle decreases, make sure that the price

00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:41.000
of the bundle is still equal to or lower than the combined price for all the products in it.

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:48.000
Bundle prices don't update automatically in response to updates in the prices of individual products.

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:54.000
So make sure you check your bundle prices when you update individual products.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:06:00.611
Or set pricing rules that keep virtual bundle prices at or below the combined price for bundled

00:06:00.611 --> 00:06:01.000
products.

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:07.333
Note too that a bundle that's priced higher than the sum of its product prices can't become a featured

00:06:07.333 --> 00:06:09.000
offer in the Amazon store.

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:14.000
Now that you know requirements and conditions for virtual bundles, let's learn how to create one.

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:19.667
All sellers who meet the requirements for virtual bundles can access the tool by hovering over brands

00:06:19.667 --> 00:06:21.000
in the main menu,

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:27.000
clicking Build Your Brand, then scrolling down and locating the virtual bundles card.

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:32.000
On the new virtual bundle page, you'll start by selecting two to five products.

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:39.500
Click the Add Products button, then in the pop-up, browse for products or enter one asin at a time

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:41.000
in the search bar.

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:46.000
Click Add to Bundle at the end of a row to make it part of the bundle.

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:50.000
The product you add first will be set as your bundle's main product.

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:56.261
When you're finished adding products, click the Done Adding Products button to return to the new

00:06:56.261 --> 00:06:59.000
virtual bundle page with your products populated.

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:05.906
Next, underneath your bundle's product list, click Select Images and Layout to go to a second pop-

00:07:05.906 --> 00:07:12.000
up where you'll upload a main image for your bundle and select Additional Product Images.

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:17.542
For your main image, click the Browse button to upload a new image that shows each product in your

00:07:17.542 --> 00:07:19.000
bundle against a white background.

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:25.667
For your additional images, you can either click Upload a New Image or Select Images that are already

00:07:25.667 --> 00:07:29.000
on the product detail pages for your individual products.

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:36.000
Click the Save button to return to the new virtual bundle page with your images populated.

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:42.955
Finally, enter a full title, a short title, a price, a description, bullet points and an optional

00:07:42.955 --> 00:07:45.000
SKU for your virtual bundle.

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:52.500
We recommend a brief descriptive bundle title that names the main product and additional products,

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:55.000
for example, Shampoo Plus Conditioner.

00:07:55.000 --> 00:08:00.000
Your short title is what displays in spaces that are too small for your full title.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:06.000
Try abbreviating your full title by eliminating accessory products or shortening words.

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:12.000
Remember that your price needs to be equal to or lower than the combined price for your products,

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:14.000
which we display to the right.

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:20.263
Your description and bullet points should be in the same format used on product detail pages for

00:08:20.263 --> 00:08:21.000
individual products.

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:24.000
But make sure to highlight what's in your bundle.

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:30.769
Use complete sentences for the description and start each bullet with a short phrase that identifies

00:08:30.769 --> 00:08:35.000
a value, followed by a fragment that offers additional information.

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:38.000
You don't have to enter a SKU for a bundle.

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:45.600
If you leave this field blank, we'll create one on your behalf, along with a unique asin for the

00:08:45.600 --> 00:08:46.000
bundle.

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:49.000
But if you do enter a SKU, make sure it's unique.

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:56.000
Don't reuse a SKU from an individual product within the bundle or from any other part of your catalog.

00:08:56.000 --> 00:09:01.667
After entering each piece of information for your bundle, click the Save and Publish button to create

00:09:01.667 --> 00:09:02.000
it.

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:08.000
A new virtual bundle usually appears in the Amazon store within 24 hours.

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:11.000
It'll link to the individual products in your bundle.

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:17.333
And the product detail page for the main product may also link to your new virtual bundle from a

00:09:17.333 --> 00:09:19.000
Make It a Bundle widget.

00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:26.000
If you need to update an existing bundle, hover over Inventory in the main menu in Seller Central,

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:29.000
then click Manage All Inventory.

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:35.000
Locate the bundle, which will be listed with your other products, with bundle as its status.

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:41.581
You can update the price, title, description, bullet points, and images, but you won't be able to

00:09:41.581 --> 00:09:47.000
update the products in the bundle, adjust the main product, or change the SKU.

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:54.000
If you need to update these attributes, delete your bundle, then recreate it using a different SKU,

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:59.000
or recreate it using the same SKU after 24 hours have passed.

00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:02.000
This concludes our training on virtual bundles.

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:08.303
We encourage you to watch our Seller University video on the Brand Analytics Market Basket Analysis

00:10:08.303 --> 00:10:14.606
Report if you'd like help determining which products in your brand catalog might make an effective

00:10:14.606 --> 00:10:15.000
bundle.

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:19.000
Thank you, and happy selling in the Amazon Store!
